<h1>About VisitSheet</h1>
<p>VisitSheet helps a person, or someone helping them, put one appointment on a single page: the three questions that matter most, notes in their own words, the medicine list exactly as typed, and how they want the clinic to communicate.</p>
<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Ranks your questions and boxes the first three.</li>
  <li>Keeps notes since last time, in your words, with a bother number you choose from 0 to 10.</li>
  <li>Lists medicines exactly as you typed them.</li>
  <li>Prints a one-page brief, a large-print version, and a JSON download of the same words.</li>
  <li>Offers questions you did not mark as asked last time, so you can add them with one click.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What it does not do</h2>
<ul>
  <li>It does not diagnose.</li>
  <li>It does not give medical advice.</li>
  <li>It does not check medicines or suggest treatment.</li>
  <li>It does not interpret the bother number.</li>
  <li>It is not for emergencies.</li>
</ul>
<p>All demo data is fictional. There are no real patients, clinics, clinicians, or medicine brands in the sample.</p>
<p>Each login receives its own private copy of that fictional data, so one person’s edits stay on their login.</p>
<%- include('partials/close') %>
